ext": "Tadao Takashima (1930-2019) was a renowned Japanese actor, best known for his iconic roles in Japanese cinema and television."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 143, "end": 164, "text": "Early Life and Career"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 166, "end": 308, "text": "Born on February 27, 1930, in Tokyo, Japan, Takashima began his acting career in the 1950s, appearing in numerous stage productions and films."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 309, "end": 487, "text": "He gained widespread recognition for his portrayal of the titular character in the 1960s television series \"Kaito Yabuki,\" which earned him a loyal fan base and critical acclaim."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 488, "end": 501, "text": "Personal Life"}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 503, "end": 645, "text": "Takashima's personal life was marked by a significant milestone when he married Evelyn Herbert Webb, a member of the British peerage, in 1965."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 646, "end": 811, "text": "The couple met while Takashima was on a promotional tour in London, and their whirlwind romance culminated in a private ceremony at Webb's family estate in Scotland."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 812, "end": 834, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 836, "end": 935, "text": "Several studies have explored the cultural significance of Takashima's marriage to Webb, including:"}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 937, "end": 1038, "text": "* \"Transnational Celebrity Marriages: A Case Study of Tadao Takashima and Evelyn Herbert Webb\" by Dr."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1039, "end": 1088, "text": "Yuka Nakamura (Journal of Japanese Studies, 2010)"}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1089,